Employee Performance Analysis- Business Requirements Document (BRD)
1. Project Overview
Project Name: Employee Performance Analysis
Project Type: HR Analytics / Data Analytics

Tools & Technologies:
- Python (Google Colab)
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Microsoft Power BI
- DAX

Dataset Size: 50,000 employee records after removing completely empty rows.

2. Business Problem Statement

Human Resource (HR) departments manage large amounts of employee information, including job roles, departments, performance scores, education levels, employee demographics, attrition and promotion details.
Analyzing this information manually can make it difficult to identify workforce patterns and understand employee performance across different departments.
The organization requires an interactive HR analytics solution to explore employee performance, workforce distribution, attrition patterns and promotion-related trends.

3. Business Objectives
The main objectives of this project are:

1. Analyze employee distribution across departments and job titles.
2. Evaluate employee performance using performance scores.
3. Understand workforce demographics based on gender and education level.
4. Identify performance patterns across different employee categories.
5. Analyze employee attrition trends.
6. Explore employee promotion patterns.
7. Develop an interactive Power BI dashboard to support HR analysis and decision-making.

4. Stakeholders
Primary Stakeholder: Human Resources (HR) Department

Other Stakeholders:
- HR Managers
- Department Managers
- Senior Management
- Business Decision-Makers

5. Business Requirements

Requirement ID -  Business Requirement 
BR01 | Analyze total employee distribution.
BR02 | Analyze employees across different departments.
BR03 | Evaluate employee performance scores.
BR04 | Analyze workforce distribution by job title.
BR05 | Explore gender and education-level distribution.
BR06 | Analyze employee attrition patterns.
BR07 | Explore employee promotion trends.
BR08 | Provide interactive filters for employee analysis.

6. Key Business Questions

1. Which department has the highest number of employees?
2. How are employees distributed across different job titles?
3. How does employee performance vary across performance score categories?
4. Which departments have different workforce compositions?
5. What is the gender distribution across the organization?
6. What education levels are most common among employees?
7. What patterns can be identified in employee attrition?
8. How are employee promotions distributed?

7. Project Scope
- Employee data cleaning and preprocessing.
- Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA).
- Employee performance analysis.
- Department and job-title analysis.
- Attrition and promotion analysis.
- Interactive Power BI dashboard development.

Out of Scope:
- Predicting future employee performance.
- Predicting employee resignation.
- Making individual employee promotion decisions.
- Evaluating employee performance without appropriate business-approved criteria.

8. Expected Deliverables
- Cleaned employee dataset.
- Python data cleaning and analysis notebook.
- Exploratory Data Analysis.
- Interactive Power BI dashboard.
- Business insights and recommendations.
- GitHub project documentation.

9. Expected Business Value
The project aims to help HR teams explore employee information, understand workforce distribution, investigate performance patterns and identify areas
requiring further attention.

The interactive dashboard provides a consolidated view of HR-related metrics to support data-driven discussions and decision-making.
